# Wrangler `.dev.vars` template — copy to `.dev.vars` for local development.
#
# `wrangler dev` (including the workerd-backed `pnpm dev` via
# `@cloudflare/vite-plugin`) auto-loads this file from the project root
# and exposes each entry as a Worker binding, mirroring `wrangler secret
# put` for production. Never commit the real `.dev.vars` — it is listed
# in `.gitignore`.
#
# Non-secret config (e.g. `APP_URL`) belongs in `wrangler.jsonc` `vars`,
# not here. Reserve this file for credentials that must not be checked
# in; an entry here overrides the same-named `vars` entry.
#
# SESSION_SECRET="at-least-32-random-characters"
#
# Real mail over SMTP (port 465, implicit TLS) instead of the development
# inbox. SMTP_PORT may be omitted; only 465 is accepted.
# MAIL_TRANSPORT="smtp"
# MAIL_FROM="Lunt <no-reply@your-domain.example>"
# SMTP_HOST="smtp.your-provider.example"
# SMTP_USERNAME="apikey-or-user"
# SMTP_PASSWORD="secret"
#
# Real Google login instead of the development fake provider. The OAuth
# client's authorized redirect URI must be
# <APP_URL>/login/external/google/callback.
# EXTERNAL_IDP="google"
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID="1234567890-abc.apps.googleusercontent.com"
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET="secret"
#
# Login mail cap: unexpired login mails one address may have at once
# (default 5; set in wrangler.jsonc vars). Lower it to try MY-02's
# 「送信の上限」 state quickly.
# LOGIN_MAX_UNEXPIRED_CHALLENGES="2"
